        "text": "All coordinates below are original source coordinates retained in the issued packet, at revision 5f00082d86768368478ed7cc85b52dd56a60255b. They are references to the shared subject packet, not to private scratch.\n\n1. declaration-source.txt, report_declaration.py:43-94: _parse locates a top-level declaration fence and refuses missing/invalid fence cases. At 92-94, no declaration span produces reason missing. Prose is not interpreted as a completion claim.\n2. report_declaration.py:95-132: declaration bytes are UTF-8 decoded and parsed by loads_control; duplicate keys map to duplicate_key at 98-99. Object type, schema, exact field membership, identities and allowed claim values are checked. report_kind=None is allowed except when completion='complete'. control-json-source.txt, _json.py:20-34, supplies the duplicate-name hook: it rejects a repeated decoded key instead of selecting one of the competing values. error-source.txt, _bootstrap.py:231-241, shows diagnostics retain reason, message, retained paths and next steps rather than turning a refusal into a grade.\n3. report_declaration.py:143-147: a parser refusal becomes status missing only for reason missing; other parser refusals become invalid. Both have declaration=None and comparisons={}, with the diagnostic retained. No original invalid payload is carried in declaration, which is an intentional limit of this view.\n4. report_declaration.py:150-158: parsed identities are compared against expected values. Each comparison records expected, observed, source and matches. Any mismatch produces an identity_mismatch diagnostic and status mismatch, while retaining the parsed declaration. With all comparisons equal, status is valid and diagnostics is empty.\n5. report_declaration.py:161-170: five expectations come from the supplied session and are labeled pinned session. The observed_checkout_commit expectation is added only when collected_head is not None and is labeled HEAD observed at collection. These labels describe the stipulated sources in this study; they do not prove capture authenticity.\n6. consumer-source.txt, status.py:78-82: both claim objects receive explicit auditor attribution, source and an evidentiary note. At 92-94 the consumer obtains expectations, calls the validator, and supplies both the conditional declaration and the entire validation result to claims. This is the first apparent collapse of valid/non-valid claim values, but it is not a loss of the required distinctions: the companion validation survives inside both claim objects.\n\nThe supported inspection rule is to read reason if present, otherwise inspect validation.status, validation.diagnostics and, for binding questions, validation.comparisons and validation.declaration. Read the claim value with its attribution, source and note. The code does not establish that a manager or any later rendering actually follows this rule; the question makes the returned dictionary itself the available view."
